Flow sequence spread to K&R
description: the flow_seq_spread state
- >
  The sequence half of `flow_map_spread` - Enter puts the next element on its own row (the json5p
  concrete switch), a comma keeps it on this one, and Backspace past the closer joins the token
  back
- !!<*yamlover: $defs: table>
  header:
    - Event
      width: 2
    - 'Condition / note'
      width: 4
    - 'Next state'
      width: 2
  - ['`alphanumeric`', '', '[unquoted_scalar_appending](*::server:yamlover-editor:unquoted_scalar_appending)']
  - ['`close_bracket`', '', '[scalar_committed](*::server:yamlover-editor:scalar_committed)']
  - ['`comma`', '', '`flow_seq_spread` (stays)']
  - ['`enter`', 'otherwise', '`flow_seq_spread` (stays)']
  - ['`backspace`', 'the inner cell is empty and it is the only one', '[empty_cell_of_origin](*::server:yamlover-editor:empty_cell_of_origin)']
  - ['`backspace`', 'the caret is past the closer', '[flow_seq_editing](*::server:yamlover-editor:flow_seq_editing)']
  - ['`backspace`', 'otherwise', '`flow_seq_spread` (stays)']
